{
  "file": "crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs",
  "item": "fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]/impl[GraphWithChangingEdges/Fingerprinting]/fn[fingerprint]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "Fingerprinting is required by validation, but this regression\n observes only the outgoing-edge selection. No node contents\n are read, so producing a content fingerprint would violate the\n asserted selection-only dependencies."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `fn[fingerprint]` in `impl[GraphWithChangingEdges/Fingerprinting]` meets the built-in's criteria.\n\n- **Placement and form:** The citation is on an explicit function with a body. Its explanation is in fenced citation commentary, which the built-in accepts. The commentary is not a bare non-doc comment.\n- **Substantive reason:** The `Fingerprinting` trait requires this callback, but the test checks only an outgoing-edge dependency. The body is `panic!(\"edge inspection must not fingerprint node contents\")`, so it acts as a guard. If it ran, node contents would have been read, and that would contradict what the test asserts. That is a real reason for the function to go unexecuted, not just difficulty.\n- **Agreement with the source:** The test never gives node contents. `node_content` and `format_node_content` also panic. The test asserts that the only recorded dependency is `Dependency::OutgoingEdges(1, (), edge_fingerprint(&graph, &[2]))`. `edge_fingerprint` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs` hashes only `graph.node_path` values and does not call `Graph::fingerprint`. `InspectionContext::prepare_edges` records that edge fingerprint. So the edge path never reaches `fingerprint`, which matches the commentary.\n- **Role:** A coverage exception is the right citation here, because this function is a required-but-unreachable guard stub. It is not an implementation of a requirement or a test. The commentary doesn't also use {impl} or {test} on the same name, so nothing is redundant.",
